{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/73813-a-new-merit-faerie-form","id":73813,"title":"A New Merit: Faerie Form","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-17T11:49:20-08:00","id":73813,"title":"A New Merit: Faerie Form","content":"Several bits of fiction from the Changeling books make mention of what amount to purely cosmetic alterations to one's Mien. However, there are times when these changes engender a bit of a disconnect between narrative and mechanics. So, I've come up with the following Merit to help shore up the issue. It's probably nowhere near from perfect, so feedback would be much appreciated. Also, this might be rendered completely obsolete by a GMC update to Changeling, but I've already come to terms with that.<br /> <br /> <b>Faerie Form </b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> <br /> Changelings find that their time in Arcadia twists their bodies in strange and sometimes terrifying ways. This isn't always to their disadvantage though. A Lost's Seeming and Kith both grant her blessings from her Durance, but sometimes the Wyrd takes things a little farther. The Mien doesn't always line up perfectly with the Mask, and some changelings have learned to take advantage of this disconnect.<br /> <br /> When the Faerie Form Merit is taken, choose one: A temperature extreme, an extreme environment, a biological process, a body part. The changeling adds her Wyrd score either to resist the chosen temperature/environment, or to resist effects that target the process/organ. In cases where a value is instead subtracted from an offending dice pool, the changeling's Wyrd is instead added to that value. In cases where the changeling would already add her Wyrd to a resistance roll (such as against supernatural effects), the changeling adds the 9-again quality to her roll, and rolls where the attacker would subtract the changeling's Wyrd lose the 10-again quality.<br /> <br /> Some examples:<br /> <br /> <i>Melvin the Stonebones has inured himself to the harrowing cold after spending what felt like centuries in a realm of Eternal Winter. After an arduous flight through the Hedge to escape a local Wild Hunt, Melvin finds himself dropped off in the Alaskan tundra. As he tries to find his way back to some sort of civilization, the Storyteller calls for Melvin's player to make a Stamina + Resolve roll to resist succumbing to the arctic conditions, to which roll Melvin adds his Wyrd score of 4.<br /> <br /> Clarissa the Levinquick's nervous system is a nest of writhing, volatile wires and sparks. After her latest scheme goes awry, she finds herself facing down a Warlock who casts an Emotional Urging spell on her to fill her with fear. She normally gets to roll her Composure + Wyrd to resist; though her pool is a paltry 3 dice, thanks to her Faerie Form, her roll gains the 9-again quality, giving her a fighting chance.<br /> <br /> Harvey the Chirurgeon had his left hand replaced with a simulacrum of wicker and glass when his Keeper decided her new slave wasn't moving his fingers fast enough for her liking. Said hand now rests in a vice grip; said vice grip is in the hands of a mafia enforcer who likes neither Harvey's tone of voice, nor the fact that the Wizened has yet to pay back a single cent of the money he borrowed from the Family. Crushing Harvey's hand would be a Strength + equipment bonus roll, but because of his Mien, the enforcer loses Harvey's 3 dots of Wyrd from his roll. So much the better since Harv's sworn to operate on the Autumn King's mortal sister the next day.<br /> <br /> Sadako the Palewraith (and Northern Queen of Fukuoka) spent her maddening Durance in the Maw of Oblivion, a lightless, airless void. After she instructs her Court to shun the strange man with cuts all over his body who came to her with a thousand questions, he retaliates by sending a spirit of suffocation to draw all the breath out of her bedchamber. Because of her time without air though, Sadako adds her prodigious Wyrd score of 9 to her Stamina + Resolve roll to hold her breath in the oxygenless environment.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Like all fae defenses, Faerie Form doesn't protect its holder against cold iron. Also, this Merit's blessing can douse a changeling too much in the fantastical\u2014any time the Lost successfully resists an effect that would seem impossible to a mortal observer (such as spending hours in below-freezing temperatures while wearing shorts and a t-shirt and not developing frostbite) are cause for a Clarity 8 Breaking Point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T18:52:43-08:00","id":74020,"title":"","content":"It's interesting, but the benefits seem potentially *far* too potent for 3 points. I mean, Lethal Mein is 3 points, and it just lets you deal Lethal or gives you +1 to attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T05:15:23-08:00","id":74210,"title":"","content":"It's not much different than Dual Kith to be honest, save with a blessing that isn't directly tied to the Kith axis. I don't see the example effects as too potent for a 3 dot-er comparatively, especially given it has a drawback. The merit is fairly niche and specific, so I wouldn't use Lethal Mien as a baseline when there are others out there that can do some pretty potent things at similar dot ratings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T10:43:06-08:00","id":74373,"title":"","content":"I agree that Lethal Mien is not a good comparison (as in it is way overpriced, mostly showed how weak some of the Kith bonuses are). <br /> <br /> My only issue with what I've read is the idea that you can apparently pick an entire anatomical system as an example option. Being able to take something like &quot;nervous system&quot; is far superior to something like &quot;hand.&quot; If I could take Integument as the part protected by this, my eyes and teeth would pretty much be the only exposed part of my body not protected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T06:57:26-08:00","id":74941,"title":"","content":"I think considering the limits being a single body part or a single temperature extreme, this should be <b>Two Dots</b> (\u25cf\u25cf).<br /> <br /> Merits do not usually have such severe penalties built in... so I'd mellow out the drawback, suggestion below:<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Like all fae defenses, Faerie Form doesn't protect its holder against cold iron. Also, this Merit's blessing can douse a changeling too much in the fantastical\u2014any time the Lost successfully resists an effect that would seem impossible to a mortal observer (such as spending hours in below-freezing temperatures while wearing shorts and a t-shirt and not developing frostbite) are cause for a loss of Willpower, one point per use.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 pt Glamour<br /> <br /> <b>Catch</b>: no Glamour spent if the Changeling can use Virtue/Vice to call attention to the Faerie Form with ally/friend/motley member that day.<br /> <br /> (keep in mind you can already do temperature extremes if you are Elemental or have the Summer Eternal, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T08:13:10-08:00","id":74972,"title":"","content":"Why would this have a Cost and a Catch? It's a Merit, not a Contract.<br /> <br /> I also don't see the justification for dropped the price and the drawback. If you think the possible Clarity check is significantly harsh, then it would make more sense for it to be cheaper. If you make the drawback less harsh, than there's less reason to drop the price.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T12:13:31-08:00","id":75124,"title":"","content":"OK, you're right, I was not clear. I think Merits are almost always positive traits. What I did not say was that the description struck me more of the format of a Contract that had some situational advantage with a penalty associated with it.<br /> <br /> Clarity loss seems a harsh way to frame a Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T14:30:26-08:00","id":75214,"title":"","content":"Plenty of Merits have drawbacks. The idea though is that the positives outweigh the negatives and the cost should probably reflect the drawback being hefty if it is.<br /> <br /> I can understand why you'd look at this like a Contract, but realistically speaking those Contracts already exist (for the most part, there's no Contract for making your hand harder to damage, but there are plenty of environmental/etc. resistance ones). I believe the OP's goal is a Merit that reflects a changeling who's body has been significantly more altered than usual by their experiences in Arcadia; which there are plenty of similar examples of in the books.<br /> <br /> As for the Clarity bit, keep in mind that it's a Clarity 8 check; and only a check when you do the impossible/inhuman. The roll is not automatically going to happen every time the Merit is applied, and you aren't going to lose Clarity every time it is applied. Maintaining Clarity 8+ is already pretty damned hard, and you start with 7, which means you would need to spend XP on Clarity before you even have to worry about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T09:00:29-08:00","id":75658,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I see your point about the balance of power. How about instead the changeling chooses a type of damage/environmental hazard/etc to which they can add their Wyrd score to resist? So, you'd choose something like Electricity/Extreme Cold/Glass/Emotional Manipulation/Acid/Sandstorms/Called Shots To The Heart. That might step on the toes of some Contracts though (such as the first Clause of Elements).<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the changeling instead chooses a body part, adds their Wyrd to rolls to resist effects related to the organ, and subtracts their Wyrd from attackers' dice pools when they make targeted attacks against it. So, if a Mannikin has Faerie Form (Eyes), he'd add his Wyrd to resist blinding effects, and someone trying to stab him in the eye would subtract the changeling's Wyrd from his pool. It feels weirdly empirical for a game about fairy tales though. I wonder if symbolic effects should be resistible as well. Maybe you choose the organ, and then one effect, either physical or symbolic, that the Merit protects you from. So if you have Faerie Form (Heart), you'd have the protection against attacks that target your heart, and then you'd choose an additional resistance, something like either effects that manipulate your blood, or effects that manipulate your desires. Also, if you choose something like Faerie Form (Skin), the targeted attack resistance only works against attacks that really do only specifically target your skin (being shot doesn't count, but scalping would).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T13:39:50-08:00","id":75854,"title":"","content":"Yes, now that interpretation sounds pretty interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T23:15:49-08:00","id":76885,"title":"","content":"That's actually quite a cool idea. The fact that it's a resistance instead of an outright immunity also means it doesn't step on the toes of things like Elements 1 and whatnot, especially because it hits different areas (Elements being environment but not weaponised Element for example, but this works for combat areas).<br /> <br /> It's like Arcadian Body, minus the cheesiness :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T12:46:32-08:00","id":77274,"title":"","content":"^ Honestly, I like this merit a lot better than Arcadian Body. Arcadian Body is good from a more power-focused mechanic perspective, i.e. trying to build a character who's better, faster, stronger, but it doesn't have as much flavor as this one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I like the drawback, too~<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T08:58:56-08:00","id":82661,"title":"","content":"The drawback as described makes me wonder why it threatens the characte's clarity, rather than causing the potential revealing of the Mask. Maybe everyone else just plays the game differnt than me, but when mortals see a changeling doing something supernatural, I treat that as a potential to reveal the fae's trye nature to the mortal's senses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I also post a long form story, based on a Changeling: The Lost campaign at: <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10018173/1/Great-Fight-A-Twilight-Tommy-Tale\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1001817...ght-Tommy-Tale</a><br /> I hope you will enjoy it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2020-gitariart","name":"GitariArt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T11:01:35-08:00","id":82697,"title":"","content":"I believe the intent is that it challenges the changeling's sense of normalcy. It doesn't matter if other people see you do it or not, you know you survived the impossible because you're made of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T12:51:52-08:00","id":84150,"title":"","content":"Pretty much what Heavy Arms said; it's very personal. It's hard to keep all things Fae (and being able to seperate Fae insanity from reality) in check when you're making a nose-dive into it further in a tangible, undeniable way. That actually makes more sense to me than witnesses impacting it for that merit.<br /> <br /> Honestly though, I've always wondered why others witnessing it actually mattered worth a damn in the clarity char; I could see the case being made that others witnessing (and responding) to the strangeness validates and reinforces that you're not normal anymore though, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Edit: also, I like the revision suggestions to the merit (namely it being a 2 dot among some others), I'd be willing to use this one without much guff over Arcadian Body; it seems to dovetail well with Lethal Mien and similar altering merits to customize a character further into the land of &quot;I'm really, REALLY messed up from my time in Faerie&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":". 03-04-2014, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T08:47:59-07:00","id":90924,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback. I need to mull over this some more.<br /> <br /> Suggested changes:<ul><li>Make it less expensive.</li> <li>Work in the other revisions.</li> <li>Re-examine level of Clarity loss. (Maybe 7 instead of 8? That way it's not as much of a non-issue. That might also make it less appealing though.)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T19:23:50-07:00","id":92573,"title":"","content":"Honestly, this is more of an Exalted wyld mutants kind of thing. I would look at that system and try to transplant it. Instead of pigeonholing it into a merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}